1. If the world contains *any* generative AI content, it should be flagged as such. The problem isn't the volume used, it's the fact that it's morally bankrupt from the very beginning. We should have the ability to assess content in our experiences, go "Nah, I don't want to give this any traction", and find something genuine and heartfelt instead.

2. If you use AI because you ramble, then ramble! What you actually have to say is a *billion* times more valuable and welcome that some sanitised AI summary.
